 "title": "Breakbeat",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: a funky, syncopated breakbeat: the kick skipping around the bar, the snare hard on 2 and 4, busy sixteenth hats, the backbone of big beat and breaks. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock. Two Sequencers on eighths: the kick's has steps 1, 4 and 6 on (the 'and' of 2 and of 3: the syncopation), the snare's steps 3 and 7. Hats on every 1/16. Drive gives the loop some dirt; a short Reverb.\n\nTweak: switch kick steps on and off (that's how breakbeats are written), TEMPO (try 95 and 140), DRIVE.",
